From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 10:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] include: l_stdlib: do not redeclare memchr with newer glibc

With newer glibc headers, `memchr` may already be provided as a fortified
macro using `_Generic`. The legacy fallback declaration in `l_stdlib.h` then
expands through that macro and causes a compile failure in the SNTP build.

Skip the fallback declaration when `memchr` is already defined as a macro.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [glibc compatibility]
Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 include/l_stdlib.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/l_stdlib.h b/include/l_stdlib.h
index 18d8557..20d34da 100644
--- a/include/l_stdlib.h
+++ b/include/l_stdlib.h
@@ -221,7 +221,7 @@ extern	int	h_errno;
 extern	int	h_errno;
 #endif
 
-#ifndef HAVE_MEMCHR
+#if !defined(HAVE_MEMCHR) && !defined(memchr)
 extern void *memchr(const void *s, int c, size_t n);
 #endif
 
-- 
2.43.0
